      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-312592",
      ":question/problem": "Two identical wooden blocks are each in the shape of a cylinder with a height of $15$ centimeters. The surface area of each block is $M$ square centimeters. When the two blocks are joined together by gluing one of their bases together, the resulting solid has a surface area of $1.2M$ square centimeters. What is the radius, in centimeters, of each circular base?\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that the surface area $S$ of a cylinder is given by*\n$S|= 2 \\cdot (base area) + (lateral surface area); = 2 \\cdot \u03c0r^{2} + 2\u03c0rh$\n*where $r$ is the base radius and $h$ is its height.*"
    }
